-{"id":"DF-0919-01","status":"pending","priority":"P1","complexity":2,"title":"P1 - fresh install on an empty store: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile does not link ~30 root-level packages (express among them); daemon boot dies with Cannot find module 'express'","reasoning":"Dogfood 09-19 ephemeral bunker (las-bunker-03 agent 7649b92c, clean Debian user, node 22.23.2, pnpm 12.4.2 via corepack): clone ce936ae + pnpm install --frozen-lockfile RC=0 in 60s, but node_modules/ had only 9 top-level links and `node bin/duckbrain.js http` failed `Cannot find module 'express'` (require stack src/cli/http.ts <- bin/duckbrain.ts). express@5.2.1 IS in pnpm-lock.yaml importers (line 26) AND in node_modules/.modules.yaml hoistedDependencies, yet no symlink. `pnpm add express@5.2.1` repaired it (rewrote package.json+lockfile) and the daemon then booted health 200. This is a pnpm isolated-linker state bug on fresh stores, distinct from closed DOGFOOD-0904-02 (express was not declared - now fixed). Suspects: pnpm 12 + lockfileVersion 9 isolated linker, or the unfiltered packages/ui importer in the lockfile. Fix direction: reproduce with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` on an empty store vs `pnpm install`; consider pinning pnpm major in packageManager field; add a fresh-install smoke to CI that actually boots the daemon (not just install RC=0)."}
-{"id":"DF-0919-02","status":"pending","priority":"P1","complexity":1,"title":"P1 - pnpm build fails on a fresh clone: packages/ui/tsconfig.json:18 has `baseUrl`, removed in TypeScript 7 (TS5102)","reasoning":"Same bunker run: after install, `pnpm build` (npm run build --prefix packages/ui -> tsc && vite build) fails immediately: tsconfig.json(18,5): error TS5102: Option 'baseUrl' has been removed. Use '\"paths\": {\"*\": [\"./*\"]}' instead. Lockfile resolves typescript ^7.0.0 -> 7.0.2. Dev checkouts with stale node_modules (pre-TS7) never run this leg, so the break was invisible locally. Fix: delete the baseUrl line from packages/ui/tsconfig.json (TS7 paths resolve relative to the tsconfig without it), then verify `pnpm install && pnpm build` from a truly fresh clone in CI."}
-{"id":"DF-0919-03","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":1,"title":"P2 - README prerequisites version drift: says pnpm 11+, fresh corepack installs pnpm 12.4.2; corepack enable needs --install-directory on non-root boxes","reasoning":"README line 74: 'You need git, Node.js 22+ and pnpm 11+'. Bunker corepack defaulted to pnpm 12.4.2 and bare `corepack enable pnpm` died with EACCES trying to symlink into /usr/bin (no sudo on a fresh user) - it needs `corepack enable pnpm --install-directory ~/.local/bin`. Update README: exact verified pnpm major, plus the non-root corepack one-liner, so the first command a fresh user runs does not error."}
