 {"id":"DF-0919-04","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"title":"P3 - /health returns 503 degraded while every active embedding provider is healthy: keyless openai provider counts as unhealthy","reasoning":"Scratch daemon (fresh clone, no DUCKBRAIN_EMBEDDING_API_KEY): /health shows provider lmstudio healthy:true, ollama healthy:true, openai healthy:false 'missing API key', aggregate degraded -> HTTP 503. A fresh user whose daemon works correctly for writes/exact/semantic recall (all verified live) reads a 503 and assumes breakage. Fix direction: exclude providers with no key/configured (or with reason 'missing API key') from the aggregate, or report configuredProviders vs total so the status code reflects actually-configured health."}
 {"id":"DF-0919-05","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":1,"title":"P3 - remember validation asymmetry: camelCase `validUntil` silently ignored, snake_case `valid_until` honored","reasoning":"Live probe 09-19 on scratch daemon: POST /api/memories with validUntil:'2026-09-01' returned 201 but the memory stayed visible in the current view and carried NO valid_until field (zod schema src/mcp/tools/remember.ts only maps valid_from/valid_until); resending as valid_until worked and the row vanished from the current view (visible via ?historical=true). Silent field-dropping means a caller using the API-spec-adjacent spelling gets unbounded retention with no error. Fix: accept both spellings or set the schema strict so unknown keys 400."}
